# Conventional Commits

Always write Git commit messages following [Conventional Commits v1.0.0](https://www.conventionalcommits.org/en/v1.0.0/).

## Format
```
<type>[optional scope]: <description>

[optional body]

[optional footer(s)>
```

## Allowed Types
- feat, fix, docs, style, refactor, perf, test, build, ci, chore, revert

## Rules
- Type and description required
- Scope optional, in parentheses
- Description: imperative mood, no trailing period
- Breaking change: `!` or `BREAKING CHANGE:` footer
- Separate body/footer with blank line
- Wrap at ~72 characters
- Link issues in footers when relevant

## Examples
- `feat: add user settings`
- `fix(api): handle 429 responses`
- `feat(auth)!: change token format` with `BREAKING CHANGE:` if needed